#Information
screen.INFORMATION=Information
screen.INFORMATION.comment=This area contains informational buttons only.

option.info0=§bHover over to view description
value.info0.0=
option.info0.comment=This area contains informational buttons only.

option.info1=How to Improve Performance
value.info1.0=
option.info1.comment=Performance in Minecraft is a complex topic affected by many factors, but you can try these: lower the render distance, most devices are recommended to set it between 6-16. Lower the "Profile" shader settings, which have been carefully tested for optimal visual/performance ratio.

option.info2=What Are the Best Settings
value.info2.0=
option.info2.comment=The best settings vary per person, but for most people the defaults are close to optimal. The default settings have been refined through years of community evaluation and feedback, with a strong emphasis on visual/performance ratio. You can still freely adjust and enjoy the process!

option.info3=What Are Profiles and Visual Styles
value.info3.0=
option.info3.comment="Profile" settings change settings in the "Performance Settings" menu but do not affect any preference-type settings. "Visual Style" changes the "Follow Style" values of many preference settings, but has little impact on performance.

option.info4=What is RP Support
value.info4.0=
option.info4.comment=The RP Support option determines how the shader pack handles different blocks in Minecraft. §bIntegrated PBR+§r treats gold blocks as reflective objects, while §elabPBR§r or §eseuspbr§r require a resource pack to inform the shader. Setting RP Support to §aBasic§r means no blocks are "special" except for a few exceptions like water.

option.info5=What Are Yellow Settings
value.info5.0=
option.info5.comment=Settings with yellow names have a significant impact on performance, even though they are not in the "Performance Settings" category. If red text appears when enabled, the performance cost is very high.

option.info6=
value.info6.0=
option.info6.comment=

